## Poland — src/countries/pl/data/

Wojewodztwa (voivodeships) and powiaty (counties).

Licence: Open Data Commons Open Database License 1.0 (ODbL)
https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/
Source: (c) OpenStreetMap contributors, obtained via the geoBoundaries project
(https://www.geoboundaries.org/)

ODbL is share-alike for data: a modified version of these boundaries must be
distributed under ODbL as well, with OpenStreetMap credited. Using the package
carries no such obligation - that binds whoever changes the boundary data.

Both levels come from the same OpenStreetMap extract, which is why they register
against each other, and both are credited the same way.

Names were normalised on the way in: eleven powiaty arrived under English names
("Colberg County") and are shipped under their Polish ones, and the ten powiat
names that occur twice in Poland carry their voivodeship in brackets so that the
two are separate regions rather than one merged pair.

