## United States - src/countries/us/data/

States and the District of Columbia, and counties and county equivalents.

Licence: Public domain
Source: United States Census Bureau, MAF/TIGER database, obtained via the
geoBoundaries project (https://www.geoboundaries.org/)

Work of the US federal government carries no copyright, so there is no obligation
attached to this data. The geoBoundaries project asks to be acknowledged where
its data is used, which is why it appears in the attribution overlay alongside
the Census Bureau.

Alaska and Hawaii are moved and rescaled into inset positions, and the
Northwestern Hawaiian Islands are dropped.

## Attribution overlay

Map components render an attribution overlay by default, which is what satisfies
the attribution requirement of the licences above at runtime.

Setting `showAttributions={false}` removes it. That is permitted, but it moves
the attribution obligation onto whoever does it — they must credit the source
elsewhere in their interface or documentation.
